{"author":{"id":"417295a7cc0952a9a38b67be3a894daed91f9069f7407e038d12a4f9b9a8451e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792346763,"nonce":"WvgmdduaXLoLQgOrxGo9tMylXSM=","title":"A fiber that runs out of fuel at a call skips the call","message":"The poll before a call (Op::Call and Op::CallMethod) saved the program counter after the call, because pc is advanced at fetch. When a fiber's budget ran out exactly there, it yielded, and on its next turn went on from the instruction after the call: the call never happened and the register kept the callee. run_source gives a script 10,000 polls a turn, so any script whose loops used up the budget just before a call lost that call.\n\nReproducer: var a = [for (i in 0...10000) i]; var s = signal(a); left s holding the signal function. Found by mounting a 10,000-row list.\n\nFix: the polls before a call resume at the call. Test: the same script run at every fuel from 1 to 60 must give the same answer.","files":null}]}